{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1400023-science-fiction-being-on-the-nose","id":1400023,"title":"Science Fiction being \"on the nose?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-30T01:29:09-07:00","id":1400023,"title":"Science Fiction being \"on the nose?\"","content":"So I am thinking of an idea for a science fiction story based around some of the social issues of the day. But my idea could probably be considered to be too &quot;on the nose&quot; as they say. In regards to this...<br /> <br /> 1. Why is being too &quot;on the nose&quot; a bad thing? Why should we try to hide what our story is about?<br /> <br /> 2. How do we avoid being &quot;on the nose?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T02:31:29-07:00","id":1400028,"title":"","content":"Question on clearing things up - <b>What do you mean as 'on the nose' subject?</b> Because it can be very different things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T02:53:06-07:00","id":1400032,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I am not sure. It's a criticism I see thrown around a bit, particularly when it comes to science fiction about social issues.<br /> <br /> I have heard criticisms about Detroit: Become Human for being too &quot;on the nose&quot; in regards to commentary on slavery and civil rights. Without making this a thread about that game in particular, and whether that criticism has any merit, I am trying to figure out what that criticism really means and how to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T04:42:22-07:00","id":1400048,"title":"","content":"Early star trek and twilight zone episodes were pretty &quot;on the nose&quot; about a few subjects but still wrapped it up in enough science fiction so they weren't beating you over the head with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-30T06:05:22-07:00","id":1400066,"title":"","content":"Often the critique is meant to express that the work feels like it was made to preach first and to entertain second, and many folks don\u2019t like feeling like they\u2019re being preached to. Other times, it\u2019s used to express that an allegory is being used too literally, which can cause unintended implications. For an excellent breakdown of the latter issue, check out Jack Saint\u2019s video on Zootopia and the pitfalls of race allegory, and potentially his two subsequent videos on Beastars. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/7oR6iET6FVo\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/7oR6iET6FVo</a><br /> <br /> Without knowing more details about your story idea, it\u2019s difficult to assess what about it may be \u201con the nose\u201d and make helpful suggestions. It might be a good idea to have a sensitivity reader look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T07:57:33-07:00","id":1400312,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t really mind an \u201con the nose\u201d story, though as with Detroit: Become Human, a story\u2019s treatment of social issues might strike some as tone-deaf or even irresponsible. A less \u201con the nose\u201d story leaves more room for discussion and debate, more opportunities to find themes you can relate to, even if you don\u2019t agree with its central thesis.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re writing to address a social issue, it can help to check with people affected by the social issue, to see if there are any big red flags before you get too deep in the story.<br /> <br /> (Edit: Ah, I see the person above me referenced sensitivity readers. Same idea.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T09:58:30-07:00","id":1400335,"title":"","content":"This is a good general example of on the nose sci-fi expressed through satire.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X4RuB3gT8t0\" data-code=\"X4RuB3gT8t0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X4RuB3gT8t0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> <br /> Basically, it's making fun of a really overused twist in science fiction writing by reducing the format to 15 seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}